      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nDisables the following warning at the beginning of the engine launch:\n\n```log\nW1029 00:11:32.623000 1 torch/_opaque_base.py:6] torch._opaque_base is deprecated, use torch._custom_class_base instead\nW1029 00:11:32.623000 1 torch/_library/opaque_object.py:288] register_opaque_type is deprecated, use register_custom_class instead\nW1029 00:11:32.623000 1 torch/_library/opaque_object.py:211] typ='value' is deprecated, use typ='constant' instead\n(APIServer pid=1) INFO 10-29 00:11:47 [startup.py:38]\n(APIServer pid=1) INFO 10-29 00:11:47 [startup.py:38]        █     █     █▄   ▄█\n...\n```\n\n## Claims\n\n- torch 2.14 onwards use the new custom class API instead of pre-2.14 opaque-type API.\n- torch 2.11–2.13 keep using the old API, which is the only one available there.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidates with the existing `LayerName` coverage in CI.\n\n## Details\n\nOn torch 2.14, every vLLM process logs three deprecation warnings at import time because `LayerName` is registered through the pre-2.14 opaque-type API. This PR switches to the new names on torch >= 2.14 and keeps the old path for torch 2.11–2.13.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
